I think the floating eye/moat confirm is an excellent idea. I am not convinced
by the classical answer that you should stay alert. A good game can easily
take a very long time, and one will be tired near the end. If you want to
punish playing on then, why not remove the confirmation question from the
quit command, when you run in to a shopkeeper, when you are eating too much
etc. The only property that should be transferred from the real player to
the game character is wether he acts stupidly or not. That keeps the game
interesting and hard enough.


